#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:2
msgid "Build process overview"
msgstr "构建过程概览"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:4
msgid ""
"Once a project has been added and a build is triggered, Read the Docs "
"executes a set of :term:`pre-defined jobs <pre-defined build jobs>` to build"
" and upload documentation. This page explains in detail what happens behind "
"the scenes, and includes an overview of how you can change this process."
msgstr ""
"项目添加后触发构建时，Read the Docs 会执行一组 :term:`预定义任务 <pre-defined build jobs>` "
"来构建和上传文档。本页详细解释幕后发生的过程，并概述如何自定义此过程。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:10
msgid "Understanding the build process"
msgstr "理解构建过程"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:12
msgid ""
"Understanding how your content is built helps with debugging any problems "
"you might hit. It also gives you the knowledge to customize the build "
"process."
msgstr "理解内容如何构建有助于调试可能遇到的任何问题。它还能让你掌握自定义构建过程的知识。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:17
msgid ""
"All the steps are run inside a Docker container, using the image defined in "
":ref:`config-file/v2:build.os`. The build has access to all :doc:`pre-"
"defined environment variables </reference/environment-variables>` and "
":doc:`custom environment variables </environment-variables>`."
msgstr ""
"所有步骤都在 Docker 容器中运行，使用 :ref:`config-file/v2:build.os` 中定义的镜像。构建可访问所有 "
":doc:`预定义环境变量 </reference/environment-variables>` 和 :doc:`自定义环境变量 "
"</environment-variables>`。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:20
msgid "The build process includes the following jobs:"
msgstr "构建过程包含以下任务："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst
msgid "checkout"
msgstr "checkout"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:24
msgid ""
"Checks out a project's code from the Git repository. On |com_brand|, this "
"environment includes the SSH deploy key that gives access to the repository."
msgstr "从 Git 仓库检出项目代码。在 |com_brand| 上，此环境包含提供仓库访问权限的 SSH 部署密钥。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst
msgid "system_dependencies"
msgstr "system_dependencies"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:30
msgid ""
"Installs operating system and runtime dependencies. This includes specific "
"versions of a language (e.g. Python, Node.js, Go, Rust) and also ``apt`` "
"packages."
msgstr "安装操作系统和运行时依赖。包括特定版本的语言（如 Python、Node.js、Go、Rust）和 ``apt`` 包。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:33
msgid ""
":ref:`config-file/v2:build.tools` can be used to define a language version, "
"and :ref:`config-file/v2:build.apt_packages` to define ``apt`` packages."
msgstr ""
"可使用 :ref:`config-file/v2:build.tools` 定义语言版本，:ref:`config-"
"file/v2:build.apt_packages` 定义 ``apt`` 包。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst
msgid "create_environment"
msgstr "create_environment"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:38
msgid ""
"Creates a Python environment to install all the dependencies in an isolated "
"and reproducible way. Depending on what's defined by the project, a "
":term:`virtualenv` or a :ref:`conda environment <config-file/v2:conda>` will"
" be used."
msgstr ""
"创建一个 Python 环境，以隔离且可复现的方式安装所有依赖。根据项目定义，将使用 :term:`virtualenv` 或 :ref:`conda "
"环境 <config-file/v2:conda>`。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:44 ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:60
msgid ""
"This step is only executed if the :ref:`config-file/v2:sphinx` or :ref"
":`config-file/v2:mkdocs` keys are defined."
msgstr "仅当定义了 :ref:`config-file/v2:sphinx` 或 :ref:`config-file/v2:mkdocs` 键时才执行此步骤。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst
msgid "install"
msgstr "install"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:48
msgid ""
"Installs :doc:`default and project dependencies </build-default-versions>`. "
"This includes any requirements you have configured in :ref:`config-"
"file/v2:requirements file`."
msgstr ""
"安装 :doc:`默认及项目依赖 </build-default-versions>`。包括你在 :ref:`config-"
"file/v2:requirements file` 中配置的任何 requirements。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:51
msgid ""
"If the project has extra Python requirements, :ref:`config-"
"file/v2:python.install` can be used to specify them."
msgstr "如果项目有额外的 Python 依赖，可使用 :ref:`config-file/v2:python.install` 指定。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:56
msgid ""
"We strongly recommend :doc:`pinning all the versions </guides/reproducible-"
"builds>` required to build the documentation to avoid unexpected build "
"errors."
msgstr "我们强烈建议 :doc:`固定构建文档所需的所有版本 </guides/reproducible-builds>`，以避免意外的构建错误。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst
msgid "build"
msgstr "build"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:64
msgid ""
"Runs the main command to build the documentation for each of the formats "
"declared (:ref:`config-file/v2:formats`). It will use Sphinx (:ref:`config-"
"file/v2:sphinx`) or MkDocs (:ref:`config-file/v2:mkdocs`) depending on the "
"project."
msgstr ""
"运行主命令为每种声明的格式（:ref:`config-file/v2:formats`）构建文档。根据项目使用 Sphinx（:ref:`config-"
"file/v2:sphinx`）或 MkDocs（:ref:`config-file/v2:mkdocs`）。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst
msgid "upload"
msgstr "upload"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:69
msgid ""
"Once the build process finishes successfully, the resulting artifacts (HTML,"
" PDF, etc.) are uploaded to our servers. Our :doc:`CDN </reference/cdn>` is "
"then purged so your docs are *always up to date*."
msgstr ""
"构建过程成功完成后，生成的产物（HTML、PDF 等）将上传到我们的服务器。我们的 :doc:`CDN </reference/cdn>` "
"随后会被清除，确保你的文档*始终是最新的*。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:75
msgid ":doc:`/build-customization`"
msgstr ":doc:`/build-customization`"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:76
msgid ""
"Run user-defined commands if you require additional build steps or "
"customization."
msgstr "如果你需要额外的构建步骤或定制，请运行用户定义的命令。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:78
msgid ":doc:`/guides/build/direct-upload`"
msgstr ":doc:`/guides/build/direct-upload`"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:79
msgid ""
"Build the documentation in your own continuous integration pipeline and "
"upload the result to Read the Docs."
msgstr "在你自己的持续集成流水线中构建文档，并将结果上传到 Read the Docs。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:82
msgid "Skipping builds"
msgstr "跳过构建"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:84
msgid ""
"A *skipped* build is a build that is never triggered. Using :doc:`automation"
" rules </automation-rules>` with webhook filters, you can tell Read the Docs"
" to only trigger builds when something relevant has changed, for example "
"when files under ``docs/`` were modified, or when the commit message doesn't"
" contain ``[skip ci]``."
msgstr ""
"*跳过的* 构建是从未被触发的构建。结合 Webhook 过滤器使用 :doc:`自动化规则 </automation-rules>`，你可以告诉 "
"Read the Docs 仅在发生相关变更时触发构建，例如 ``docs/`` 下的文件被修改、或提交信息不包含 ``[skip ci]`` 时。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:90
msgid ""
"Skipped builds don't appear in your build history and don't consume build "
"time. This is the recommended way to avoid unnecessary builds."
msgstr "跳过的构建不会出现在构建历史中，也不消耗构建时间。这是避免不必要构建的推荐方式。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:95
msgid ":ref:`automation-rules:Webhook filters`"
msgstr ":ref:`automation-rules:Webhook filters`"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:96
msgid "Filter builds by changed files, commit message, or pull request labels."
msgstr "按变更的文件、提交信息或 Pull Request 标签过滤构建。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:98
msgid ":doc:`/guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds`"
msgstr ":doc:`/guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds`"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:99
msgid "Examples of skipping and cancelling builds based on conditions."
msgstr "基于条件跳过和取消构建的示例。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:102
msgid "Cancelling builds"
msgstr "取消构建"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:104
msgid ""
"A *cancelled* build is a build that was triggered as usual, but was stopped "
"before it finished. Cancelled builds appear in your build history with the "
"*Cancelled* state. Cancelling builds allows your team to speed up review "
"times and also help us reduce server costs and our environmental footprint."
msgstr ""
"*取消的* 构建是正常触发但未完成就停止的构建。取消的构建会以*已取消* "
"状态出现在构建历史中。取消构建可让你的团队加快审查速度，也有助于我们降低服务器成本和环境足迹。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:109
msgid "A couple common reasons you might want to cancel builds are:"
msgstr "你可能想取消构建的几个常见原因："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:111
msgid "the build has an external dependency that hasn't been updated"
msgstr "构建有未更新的外部依赖"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:112
msgid ""
"your Git provider doesn't support webhook filters, and you want to stop "
"builds when there were no changes on the documentation files"
msgstr "你的 Git 服务商不支持 Webhook 过滤器，且你想在文档文件无变更时停止构建"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:115
msgid "Read the Docs supports three different mechanisms to cancel a running build:"
msgstr "Read the Docs 支持三种取消正在运行构建的机制："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst
msgid "Manually"
msgstr "手动"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:119
msgid ""
"Project administrators can go to the build detail page and click "
":guilabel:`Cancel build`."
msgstr "项目管理员可前往构建详情页面，点击 :guilabel:`Cancel build`。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst
msgid "Automatically"
msgstr "自动"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:124
msgid ""
"When Read the Docs detects a push to a version that is already building, it "
"cancels the running build and starts a new build using the latest commit."
msgstr "当 Read the Docs 检测到已在构建的版本有新推送时，会取消正在运行的构建，并使用最新提交启动新构建。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst
msgid "Programmatically"
msgstr "编程方式"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:129
msgid ""
"You can use user-defined commands on ``build.jobs`` or ``build.commands`` "
"(see :doc:`build-customization`) to check for your own cancellation "
"condition and then return exit code ``183`` to cancel a build. You can exit "
"with the code ``0`` to continue running the build."
msgstr ""
"你可以在 ``build.jobs`` 或 ``build.commands`` 上使用用户定义的命令（见 :doc:`build-"
"customization`）检查自己的取消条件，并返回退出码 ``183`` 取消构建。退出码 ``0`` 则继续运行构建。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:133
msgid ""
"When this happens, Read the Docs will notify your :doc:`Git provider "
"</reference/git-integration>` the build succeeded (✅), so the pull request "
"doesn't have any failing checks."
msgstr ""
"发生这种情况时，Read the Docs 会通知你的 :doc:`Git 服务商 </reference/git-integration>` "
"构建成功（✅），这样 Pull Request 就不会有失败的检查。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:138
msgid ""
"Take a look at the :doc:`/guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds` page for some "
"examples."
msgstr "请参阅 :doc:`/guides/build/skip-or-cancel-builds` 页面查看示例。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:141
msgid "Automatic disabling of builds"
msgstr "自动禁用构建"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:143
msgid ""
"To reduce resource consumption and improve build queue times for all users, "
"Read the Docs will automatically disable builds for projects that have too "
"many consecutive failed builds on their default version."
msgstr "为减少资源消耗并改善所有用户的构建队列时间，Read the Docs 会自动为默认版本连续失败构建过多的项目禁用构建。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:146
msgid ""
"When a project has **25 consecutive failed builds** on its default version, "
"we will disable builds for the project."
msgstr "当项目在默认版本上有**连续 25 次失败构建** 时，我们将为该项目禁用构建。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:149
msgid ""
"This helps ensure that projects with persistent build issues don't consume "
"resources that could be used by active projects."
msgstr "这有助于确保有持续构建问题的项目不会消耗本可供活跃项目使用的资源。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:153
msgid ""
"This only applies to the default version of a project. Builds on other "
"versions (branches, tags, pull requests) are not counted towards this limit."
msgstr "这仅适用于项目的默认版本。其他版本（分支、标签、Pull Request）的构建不计入此限制。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:156
msgid ""
"If your project has been disabled due to consecutive build failures, you'll "
"need to re-enable from your project settings. Make sure to fix the "
"underlying issue to avoid being disabled again."
msgstr "如果你的项目因连续构建失败被禁用，你需要从项目设置中重新启用。请务必修复根本问题以避免再次被禁用。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:160
msgid "Build resources"
msgstr "构建资源"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:162
msgid "Every build has limited resources assigned to it. Our build limits are:"
msgstr "每个构建都有分配的资源限制。我们的构建限制如下："

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:167
msgid "|com_brand|"
msgstr "|com_brand|"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:169
msgid "30 minutes build time (upgradable)"
msgstr "30 分钟构建时间（可升级）"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:170
msgid "7GB of memory (upgradable)"
msgstr "7GB 内存（可升级）"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:171
msgid "Concurrent builds vary based on your pricing plan"
msgstr "并发构建数因定价计划而异"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:173
msgid ""
"If you are having trouble with your documentation builds, you can reach our "
"support at support@readthedocs.com."
msgstr "如果你在文档构建中遇到问题，可联系 support@readthedocs.com 获取支持。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:176
msgid "|org_brand|"
msgstr "|org_brand|"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:178
msgid "15 minutes build time"
msgstr "15 分钟构建时间"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:179
msgid "7GB of memory"
msgstr "7GB 内存"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:180
msgid "2 concurrent builds"
msgstr "2 个并发构建"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:181
msgid "5GB of disk storage (soft limit)"
msgstr "5GB 磁盘存储（软限制）"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:183
msgid ""
"We can increase build time on a per-project basis. Send an email to "
"support@readthedocs.org providing a good reason why your documentation needs"
" more resources."
msgstr "我们可按项目增加构建时间。请发送邮件至 support@readthedocs.org 并说明文档需要更多资源的充分理由。"

#: ../../upstream/docs/user/builds.rst:186
msgid ""
"If your business is hitting build limits hosting documentation on Read the "
"Docs, please consider :doc:`Read the Docs Business </commercial/index>` "
"which has options for additional build resources."
msgstr ""
"如果你的业务在 Read the Docs 托管文档时触及构建限制，请考虑 :doc:`Read the Docs Business "
"</commercial/index>`，它提供额外的构建资源选项。"

